    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0926" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/11–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-19T11:00:00+01:00">November 19,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 19—10:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>224. No acknowledgment or reply to notes delivered Nov 1 to Irish Govt<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d321-f1"/> requesting cooperation on <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Safehaven</hi> project has been received by British,
                    French or US. None of us have received intimation from External Affairs
                    officials as to de Valera’s<anchor n="42" xml:id="d321-f2"/> position. In our
                    view this forecasts unfavorable attitude …</p>
                <pb facs="0927" n="915" xml:id="pg915"/>
                <p>[The remaining portion of this telegram deals with the position of the German
                    Minister and other Germans in Ireland on repatriation of Germans from
                    Ireland.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="41" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
